  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nFew changes overall to the forecast. High pressure will continue\nto dominate through the early part of next week. A weak cold\nfront will attempt to push through the region today but with no\nmoisture. This should allow for slightly cooler temperatures\nFriday followed by a warming trend this weekend. Inverted V \nsoundings continue to show up each afternoon through the \nweekend. Momentum transfer does show the potential for a few \nstrong wind gusts this afternoon. The other issue to take into \naccount is a typical model high bias of afternoon dewpoints in \nthis pattern, RGEM model not as biased here. Yet another cold \nfront attempts to break down the ridge a bit early next week but\nalso looks moisture starved.",
